1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Posting time didn’t kill your Reel. Your first zero point eight seconds did.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Creators A-B test six o’clock against seven o’clock like it’s science. Meanwhile the hook was decided in thirty seconds at the end of the edit.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Distribution systems feed content to a test audience whenever you post. What decides the next wave isn’t your clock. It’s whether that audience stops scrolling.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
So the honest hierarchy: first second, then payoff, then save-worthiness. Posting time is a rounding error unless you’re posting at three a.m.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Send this to the friend who has a spreadsheet of posting times. They’re free now. Tomorrow: what a working first second actually contains.

